-- Q10816: C Corporations [hard/L4]
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["The IRS cannot challenge the acquisition because NOL carryforwards transfer automatically with the acquired corporation","The IRS may disallow the NOL deductions under Section 269 if the principal purpose was to obtain a tax benefit","The IRS can challenge only if the acquisition price exceeds fair market value of Thornton''s net assets","Section 269 applies only to asset acquisitions and does not cover stock purchases"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 269(a), if any person acquires control (50%+) of a corporation and the principal purpose is to obtain a deduction, credit, or allowance not otherwise available, the IRS may disallow such benefits. Westbrook''s documented intent to use Thornton''s NOLs with minimal business purpose supports disallowance.
