-- Q10832: Partnerships [easy/L1]
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["The partner''s proportionate share of total partnership liabilities","The partner''s individual bank account used for partnership transactions","A record tracking a partner''s equity based on contributions, distributions, and income or loss","The cumulative total of cash the partner has contributed over time"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under Treas. Reg. Section 1.704-1(b)(2)(iv), a partner''s capital account tracks their equity stake in the partnership. It is increased by contributions and allocated income, and decreased by distributions and allocated losses.
Wrong (A): A partner''s share of liabilities affects outside basis under Section 752, not the capital account.
Wrong (B): A partner''s personal bank account is not a tax concept and has no bearing on partnership equity tracking.
Wrong (D): Capital accounts reflect more than cash contributions; they also include property contributions, income allocations, and distributions.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 10832;

-- Q10843: Partnerships [easy/L2]
