  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Section 704(d), a partner cannot deduct losses exceeding their outside basis. The $15,000 excess is suspended and carried forward indefinitely until Chambers''s basis increases through income allocations, contributions, or increased liability share.
Wrong (A): Basis-limited losses are not permanently disallowed; they are suspended with no expiration period.
Wrong (B): The loss is allocated to Chambers on Form 1065 but deductibility is limited on her individual return.
Wrong (D): Suspended ordinary losses retain their character and do not convert to capital losses.$EXPL$
