  choices = $EXPL$["$1,700, the maximum refundable ACTC per child for 2026","$2,000, because the full unused CTC converts to a refund","$3,375, computed as 15% of earned income above $2,500","$800, the standard refundable amount allowed per qualifying child"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Section 24(d), the ACTC equals the lesser of the unused CTC or 15% of earned income above $2,500, capped at $1,700 per child. Franklin''s formula yields 15% x ($25,000 - $2,500) = $3,375, but the refundable portion is capped at $1,700.
Wrong (B): The full $2,000 CTC is not entirely refundable; only up to $1,700 may be refunded as the ACTC.
Wrong (C): While $3,375 is the formula result, the ACTC is capped at $1,700 per qualifying child.
