-- Q11008: Individual Taxation: Deductions [easy/L1]
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["AGI minus the greater of standard or itemized deductions, minus QBI deduction if applicable","Gross income minus itemized deductions only, with no other adjustments","AGI minus above-the-line deductions, without further subtractions","Gross income minus the standard deduction, then minus all tax credits"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Sections 63 and 199A, taxable income equals AGI minus the greater of the standard deduction or itemized deductions, minus the qualified business income deduction if applicable. This formula sequence (gross income to AGI to taxable income) is fundamental to individual tax computation.
Wrong (B): Taxable income starts from AGI, not gross income, and taxpayers may choose the standard deduction instead of itemizing.
Wrong (C): Above-the-line deductions are already subtracted to arrive at AGI and are not deducted again from AGI.
Wrong (D): Tax credits reduce tax liability, not taxable income, and the computation starts from AGI rather than gross income.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11008;

