  choices = $EXPL$["Yes, because the joint return exception applies when filed solely to claim a refund with no liability","No, because a married dependent filing jointly can never be claimed by another taxpayer","Yes, but only if Kendra''s gross income is below the $5,050 exemption threshold","No, because marriage automatically terminates a parent''s right to claim the child"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Section 152(b)(2), a dependent generally cannot file a joint return. However, an exception applies when the joint return is filed only to claim a refund of withheld taxes or estimated payments and neither spouse has a tax liability filing separately. Kendra and Luis meet both conditions.
