-- Q11048: Individual Taxation: Income [hard/L4]
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["$0 deductible because the entire $18,000 is suspended at the passive activity tier","$18,000 is fully deductible against Crawford''s wage income without limitation","$18,000 passes basis and at-risk limits but is fully suspended as a passive loss","$12,000 deductible with $6,000 suspended at the at-risk limitation tier"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under the three-tier framework, losses pass sequentially through basis (Section 704(d)), at-risk (Section 465), then passive activity (Section 469). Crawford''s $18,000 loss clears the $30,000 basis limit and $22,000 at-risk amount, but because he does not materially participate and has no passive income, the full $18,000 is suspended under Section 469.
